1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:02,080
Every company has a Brent.

2
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:06,720
And when Brent leaves, everything
he knew walks out the door with him.

3
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:10,160
I've worked at a bunch of
small local private companies,

4
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:14,240
and the hardest thing for all
of them wasn't sales or hiring.

5
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:16,960
It was writing down what people know.

6
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:20,760
At one place, our most senior
engineer left on a Friday.

7
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:24,060
By Monday, nobody knew how
half the system worked.

8
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:28,960
We spent weeks piecing it back together
from old emails and chat messages.

9
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:33,480
Someone leaves, and years
of context are just gone.

10
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:36,520
And the docs that do exist, stale.

11
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:37,940
Nobody trusts them.

12
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:42,480
So people just ask each
other over and over.

13
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:46,470
So I tried fixing it for
myself first: Obsidian,

14
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:48,080
Notion, all of them.

15
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:53,900
And honestly, the graphs are gorgeous,
but making them is so tedious.

16
00:00:54,020 --> 00:00:56,740
Every note, you're linking things by hand.

17
00:00:57,280 --> 00:00:59,020
It turns into a second job.

18
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:02,300
I always wished it would
just do that for me.

19
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:07,070
So I built it. It's called Corpus Wiki.

20
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:11,310
You just feed it PDFs,
Word docs, notes, screenshots,

21
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:13,820
even videos, or connect your Gmail.

22
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:16,820
It pulls out the facts and
writes the wiki for you,

23
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:19,310
every line linked to where it came from.

24
00:01:19,360 --> 00:01:22,810
And it connects everything:
the graph, the glossary,

25
00:01:22,860 --> 00:01:25,040
who's who, automatically.

26
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:26,920
No brackets, ever.

27
00:01:27,060 --> 00:01:30,570
Ask it anything, like, "Why did
we switch payment providers?"

28
00:01:30,620 --> 00:01:34,480
And it answers from what your
team actually wrote with sources.

29
00:01:34,580 --> 00:01:38,250
Drop in a newer file, and it only
rewrites the lines that changed.

30
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:41,540
And if two files disagree,
it asks you first.

31
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:45,180
A normal wiki only knows what
someone remembered to write down.

32
00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:47,060
This one keeps up on its own.

33
00:01:47,260 --> 00:01:49,280
So how does it actually work?

34
00:01:49,440 --> 00:01:55,020
Every AI step runs on open NVIDIA Nemotron
models served by Nebius Token Factory.

35
00:01:55,140 --> 00:01:57,480
Nemotron Super does the everyday work.

36
00:01:57,540 --> 00:02:01,020
It reads each upload, writes
the lines, and fact-checks them.

37
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:03,250
Nemotron Ultra makes the big calls,

38
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:05,900
like planning articles and
building the topic tree.

39
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:09,989
Nano handles the bulk linking, and the
vision model reads your screenshots,

40
00:02:10,039 --> 00:02:11,990
diagrams, and video frames.

41
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:16,450
Token Factory gives us one API for
all of them with structured output,

42
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:18,820
so every change comes back valid.

43
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:22,300
Each step gets the cheapest
model that does its job well,

44
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:24,820
and I can switch any of them in settings.

45
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,160
And when it makes a video, every render
runs as a serverless job on Nebius cloud.

46
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:34,080
And when someone leaves,
what they knew stays.

47
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:36,540
Brent's knowledge, still here.

48
00:02:37,060 --> 00:02:41,420
If your team keeps losing knowledge or
you're tired of linking notes by hand,

49
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:45,280
try it. Drop in a folder and
watch it build your brain.

50
00:02:45,460 --> 00:02:46,460
Link's below.
